# QA M6 relaxed run of Bad Ischl (D-045 measurement, ZEIT clock up to the
# goal touch, D-090). Sensible non-speedrun play at walking speed (RUN never
# held): 1.5 s at the start by the „Bus 150“ board, the M-box and its
# Mozartkugel (Zuckerschock from 350), past the Kaiser's statue and Kurgast
# #1, 4 s at the Kaiserpark terrace's edge watching file A march and
# present, past the fountain and Kurgast #2 onto the villa steps, where she
# waits 3.3 s while the Fiaker charges beneath her, the Esplanade and the
# two Traun notches with Kurgast #3, the checkpoint (0.7 s), the M-box
# (1000), the Trinkhalle, Kurgast #4 and file B, past the Kurkapelle onto
# the wall steps (1 s), the theatre balconies B1 -> B2, the Z-box bumped
# from B2 (its Zaunerstollen turns at B2's stone end pier and rolls back
# to her: ExtraLife), down past singer #2 onto the bench (0.5 s), file C,
# the Pfarrgasse, the Trafik and a walk-off to the Maibaum (100). Movement
# between the pauses: walking-only QA beam search (4-frame chunks, never
# hurt). LevelComplete at 4211; ZEIT clock consumed 4180 frames = 69.67 s:
# 3 x 69.67 = 209.0 -> 210 s (D-045, D-102).
# Re-cut for D-102 (E42), same frames and goal touch: the notch-2 leap now
# lands on the kerb (151), so the braking after it is shifted (2405-2440,
# rest at the same x); B2's stone end pier (237, rows 7-10, with the bridge
# at (236, row 8): D-102 E42 addendum) blocks the old hop over the flower
# box, so she steps left, jumps onto the box top, hops the pier and walks
# off onto the street (3475-3606); two walking jumps over singer #2 onto
# the bench (3607-3730) and a brake to the old resting x (3731-3768); from
# 3769 on her inputs and positions are the old ones.
